WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.669
From the swashbuckling Zorro to the gunslinging
mariachi, Antonio Banderas has been a household

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:07.999
name for decades.

00:00:07.999 --> 00:00:12.720
He remained a constant on our screens over
the years, reprising the role of Zorro and

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.480
joining big budget franchises in Shrek and
Spy Kids.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.100
But recently, his status as a genuine A-lister
has come into question.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:26.619
We don't really hear much from Banderas nowadays,
and here's why.

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:27.619
Typecast

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:32.310
Although Banderas took on some pretty varied
roles in his early acting days in Spain, his

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:37.090
transition to Hollywood almost immediately
pigeonholed him as the Latin lover with the

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.610
sensual voice.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:44.420
Even his actions scenes feel like he might
just start getting sexy at any minute.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.140
"Not bad."

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.000
"Not bad at all."

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.660
No matter how much makeup you put on his face
or how many things are exploding, Antonio

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.210
Banderas is never more than one tango away
from taking you to bed.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:05.450
It's a tag that's followed him his entire
career, even though he's often tried to shake

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:11.260
the typecasting with movies like Assassins,
The 13th Warrior, and 2011's The Skin I Live

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.230
In, in which he played a deranged surgeon.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:18.730
Unfortunately, critics haven't been particularly
kind to Banderas' latest work.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:24.170
Of the last ten Antonio Banderas movies reviewed
on Rotten Tomatoes, eight of them have scores

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:26.670
of less than 50 percent.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:31.400
In 2014, he turned up in The Expendables 3
looking to work on his action chops…

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.080
...but the film was bashed by critics, and
the verdict was just as bad when Banderas

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:46.610
took on the lead role in Automata later that
year.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:51.330
In their review of the apocalyptic sci-fi
film, The Wrap said that Banderas was "all

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:56.110
wrong" for the part, criticizing him for being
"shouty where he should be stern, confused

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:58.420
where he should be clued in."

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.420
Franchise player

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:06.190
When Antonio Banderas signed on to play Puss
in Boots in Shrek 2 in 2004, he probably had

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:09.850
no idea how popular the character would become.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.590
He showed up again in two more Shrek sequels
and no less than five animated specials, not

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:18.310
to mention his own spin-off prequel in 2011.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:23.600
It grossed over half a billion dollars at
the worldwide box office, but eventually the

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.330
franchise was bound to run out of steam.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:32.560
Similarly, Spy Kids finally fizzled, and Robert
Rodriguez's "Mexico Trilogy" reached its conclusion

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.460
with Once Upon a Time in Mexico.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:39.810
Antonio Banderas has plenty of other solid
film credits, but for nearly a decade, his

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:44.780
acting work rested heavily on franchises that
ultimately reached their end.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.300
But no matter what, Banderas always has a
fallback:

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.960
"You can make anything sound sexy."

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:52.680
"Really?"

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:53.420
"Okay?

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.620
And seductive."

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.040
Side gigs

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:02.430
Since 1997, Antonio Banderas has been creating
his own line of men's fragrances alongside

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.000
Spanish fashion and cosmetics giant Puig.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:10.740
In 2015, Banderas also announced that he had
signed up as a student at the famous London

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.100
fashion school Central St. Martins.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:18.350
He told the school publication, "I’m going
to continue doing movies and producing, and

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:23.310
I want to direct more – but there were other
things in my life that I was interested in."

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.640
What were those things?

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.310
If you guessed 'capes,' you'd be… yeah,
you'd be right.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.580
Antonio Banderas wants to make capes.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.700
"Zorro!

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.800
The legend has returned!"

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.370
On top of his fragrance and fashion side gigs,
Banderas is also a United Nations Development

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:47.050
Program Goodwill Ambassador and he has his
own foundation, Tears and Favors, which provides

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.880
support to cancer patients.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.870
In other words, we don't see him so much any
more because he's super busy with his commitments

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.670
away from Hollywood.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:56.670
Family time

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:02.130
In 2014, Melanie Griffith and Antonio Banderas
released a joint statement confirming that

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.780
they were bringing their near-two decades
of marriage to a close.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.319
Banderas saw this as an opportunity to turn
over a new leaf and has been busy spending

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:11.940
more time with his family.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:12.940
He told E! News:

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:17.410
"My life changed very much during the last
two years, personal reasons.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:21.989
The possibility of reinventing myself was
there, and so I said 'Probably this is the

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:23.790
moment that I can do this.'"

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:28.870
Banderas also revealed that both his step-daughter
Dakota Johnson and his biological daughter

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.080
Stella helped him get through the process.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:36.600
"I told my kids sometimes, but in fact, the
reality is I learned from them more.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.540
They were not very obedient, but I learn from
them."

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.820
Leaving Hollywood

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.780
In 2015, Banderas left the bright lights of
Hollywood for the UK countryside.

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:51.580
He currently lives with his Dutch girlfriend
Nicole Kempel in a tailor-made eco-mansion

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.510
that set him back more than $3 million.

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:58.930
Looking back, it's hardly a surprise that
Banderas chose to leave the States, as a few

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:04.040
years earlier he and his then-wife Melanie
Griffith tried to buy an apartment in world

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:10.010
famous New York apartment building "The Dakota"
only to be turned away because Banderas was

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.200
Hispanic, according to a lawsuit.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:18.270
The suit suggested that the board made cruel
jokes about Banderas upon receiving his application,

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:23.760
claiming he wanted a first floor apartment
so it would be easier to buy drugs off the

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.480
street.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.889
Health concerns

00:05:26.889 --> 00:05:32.210
In January 2017, Banderas was rushed to a
hospital near his home in England after suffering

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:35.260
"agonizing" pain in his chest during a workout.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:40.540
The Spanish star initially dismissed the incident
as an "episode" and tweeted a photo of himself

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:45.480
and girlfriend Nicole Kempel with the caption
"Enjoying nature after a little startle."

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:50.380
He later confirmed that it was indeed a heart
attack, and that he had to go under the knife

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:51.380
to fix the problem.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.940
"It was a benign attack.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:57.710
It hasn't caused a-ny permanent damage and
now I'm in a recovery period.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.250
It's something that happens every day to a
lot of people.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.240
I didn't hide it, but I didn't want it to
receive more importance than those suffered

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.350
by other people."

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:10.740
While that's great news, studio execs may
think twice before casting him in long-term

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:16.190
roles, which is a real shame for both the
actor and his fans alike.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.570
What's next?

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:21.889
One reason that Banderas chose to move out
of the spotlight was to focus on his writing.

00:06:21.889 --> 00:06:23.199
He told The Sunday Times,

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:28.350
"I am not a party person anymore so I have
the space and peace to write and really get

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.460
inside my own head.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.850
I'm working on several scripts."

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:36.580
Whether any of the screenplays he is currently
writing will come to fruition is anyone's

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:41.900
guess, but what we do know is that Banderas
hasn't given up the ghost on acting quite

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:42.900
yet.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:47.830
He'll star alongside Adrien Brody and John
Malkovich in a "Reservoir Dogs-style thriller"

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:53.889
called Unchained, play an aging rock star
in the action comedy Salty, and headling the

00:06:53.889 --> 00:06:56.300
upcoming revenge thriller Stoic.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:07:01.120
He might have been out of the picture for
a while, but Banderas looks like he has enough

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.979
left in the tank for a few more rolls of the
dice.

00:07:03.979 --> 00:07:06.860
And if that doesn't work, there's always capes!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:07.949
Thanks for watching!

00:07:07.949 --> 00:07:10.820
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:13.330
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

